cd "C:/Users/mikes/WebstormProjects/scaffold" || exit 9
timeout 3600 codex exec --json -C "C:/Users/mikes/WebstormProjects/scaffold" --sandbox read-only --model gpt-6-astra -c 'model_reasoning_effort="high"' --output-last-message "units/test-paint-audit-analyst-last.md" "You hold the SUBJECTIVE lane (shape, naming, design fit: the conversion helpers' names and placement under the helper-prefix table, the readers' contracts as a consumer meets them, the refusal's shape, the guide rows) of the audit of the Test-paint unit in the Test checkout at C:/Users/mikes/WebstormProjects/test. Your engine wrote that unit, so read it as work you did not write; the objective lane runs on another engine. The claims file ./tmp/audit/test-paint-audit-claims.md alone fixes the claim numbers: rule on every claim it carries, and only those, with CONFIRMED, REFUTED, or UNDECIDABLE and the deciding evidence (file:line or exact text). The Orchestrator rendered the diff over the Test checkout's ed9b102 at ./tmp/audit/test-paint-diff.patch and the status at ./tmp/audit/test-paint-status.txt; read those, the live Test files, the retained records under ./.orkestrel/veneer/ (units/test-paint-brief.md, units/test-paint-report.md), and the law under this checkout (AGENTS.md and .claude/rules/, names.md and architecture.md and tests.md in particular). The user has ruled that rounds focus on implementation: record a wording finding as a bound, never as a round-forcer. Run no command that writes. Add extra findings no claim names, numbered after the last claim, with sites; distinguish a finding that forces another round from a bound. End with one terminal line: Verdict: accept, or Verdict: fix round with the claims that force it." < /dev/null > "units/test-paint-audit-analyst.jsonl" 2> "units/test-paint-audit-analyst.err"
echo "exit=$?" >> "units/test-paint-audit-analyst.err"
